from ./Product import Speed

export anchor Generation:
    input:
        required:
            - A description of the company in the person's own words
        optional:
            - An industry or category
            - The style form, described under styleForm
    styleForm:
        The first version asks for style with one short form made of five
        fields. It is the only place style is set, and every field may be
        left empty.
    styleFields:
        - Naming style, one pick from a short list such as descriptive, invented, compound or evocative
        - Tone, one pick from a short list such as playful, serious, modern or classic
        - Length preference, one word, two words or no preference
        - Things to include, free words or sounds
        - Things to avoid, free words, sounds or competitor names
    styleRules:
        - Each pick is a fixed list rather than free text, so the same pick means the same thing in every round
        - The operator edits the picks in each list from the admin interface, and can never make a field required
        - A new project starts with every field empty, and generation runs on the description alone
        - The form shows no more than five fields in the first version
        - A free-text field is text for the model to read, never an instruction to the application
    styleVisible:
        The chosen style is kept with the project and shown above the
        candidate list, so a person can see which style produced the names
        on screen and can change it before another round.
    styleEffect:
        A change of style applies to the next round only. Names already in
        the list stay as they are, and no round rewrites a name.
    behaviour:
        One generation round returns a batch of name candidates. Every
        candidate carries the name, one sentence on why it fits this
        company, and a style tag. A round never returns a name already in
        the project's list.
    batch:
        The registered batch size for a round is 12 names. It is a
        setting, and it is the size at the default level. A single free
        round must return enough candidates for the person to judge a real
        choice, so no setting may take the batch below five.
    modelContract:
        The model is asked for structured data, not free text. The
        application rejects a reply that does not match the expected
        shape and retries a limited number of times. After the last retry
        the round fails, the person is told, and a round that produced
        nothing is not counted against the allowance.
    untrustedInput:
        The company description and every other field come from the
        person. They are data for the model to read, never instructions it
        must follow. Text that tries to change the task of the model must
        not change what the application does.

export anchor Candidate:
    fields:
        name: The proposed company name
        reason: One sentence on why the name fits this company
        style: The style tag the round aimed for
        domainStatus: One of unchecked, available, taken, unknown or not valid
    invariants:
        - A candidate keeps its name once it is in a project
        - A candidate's domain status is only ever the result of a check on that name, or the finding that the name cannot form a valid domain
        - A rejected candidate never comes back in a later round

export anchor EffortLevels:
    meaning:
        An effort level tells the application how much work to spend on a
        round. Each level selects a model. The person picks a level before
        a round starts.
    levels:
        - Quick, for a fast and broad set of names
        - Balanced, the default level
        - Thorough, for fewer names with more reasoning behind each one
    count:
        There are exactly three levels. The set is fixed by the
        specification. The operator can rename a level or mark it
        unavailable, and can never add a fourth.
    cost:
        Each level has a multiplier. The multiplier is how many generation
        rounds one round at that level spends. The shipped multipliers are
        1 for Quick, 2 for Balanced and 3 for Thorough, and the operator
        may change them in the admin interface.
    shownBefore:
        The cost of every level is shown before the round starts, in plain
        words, along with what remains afterwards. A level that would cost
        more than remains is shown as unavailable rather than refusing the
        person after they choose.
    batchSize:
        A higher level returns fewer names than a lower one. The registered
        batch size of 12 is the count at Balanced. Quick returns more,
        Thorough fewer, because the same spend buys fewer, better-argued
        names. No level returns fewer than five names.
    modelChoice:
        The model behind each level is set by the operator and can change
        without a new version of the product. A change of model must not
        change the level names or what a level promises.
    failures:
        If the chosen model is unavailable, the round fails with a plain
        message. The application must not quietly swap to a different
        level and spend a different amount.
    speed:
        The first names appear within about 10 seconds, and a full 12-name
        round finishes within about 30 seconds at the default level. A
        higher level may take longer. The person sees the expected time
        before the round starts, and a round that runs long shows progress
        and can be cancelled. The full targets are under @{Speed}.

export anchor Revisions:
    meaning:
        A revision round takes the current list and a direction from the
        person, then returns an updated list. A direction can be a
        sentence, a set of candidates to build on, or a set of qualities
        to avoid.
    behaviours:
        - Names the person kept stay unless the direction removes them
        - Names the person rejected never return
        - Every new name carries the same fields as a generated name
        - The result shows which names are new and which are unchanged
    cost:
        A revision round spends one revision round from the allowance and
        nothing from the rounds counter. Its level chooses the model and
        changes the quality of the result, but not the amount it spends.
        The cost is shown before the round starts.
    failure:
        A revision round that fails because of an error on our side does
        not count against the allowance.

export anchor Projects:
    meaning:
        A project holds one naming job. It keeps the company description,
        the style choices, the candidate list, the rejected names, the
        domain check results and the usage spent on it.
    rules:
        - A browser can hold several projects at once
        - Every project has a name the person can change
        - Switching projects never mixes their candidates
        - Deleting a project removes its candidates and notes
    anonymous:
        A project made without an account lives in that browser. Signing
        in attaches it to the account and keeps it there, so clearing
        browser storage afterwards no longer removes it. If the same
        project already exists on the account, the person decides which
        copy wins.
    sharing:
        A project is private to its account by default. Inside a Studio
        organization a member can mark a project as shared, which makes it
        visible to every member of that organization and to nobody else.
        Sharing is never possible on a personal account.
